  "notes": "\"The father of that guitar-driven kind of pop sound\" — acoustic guitars where the era's default was synths. 96–130 straight, backbeat on 2&4. Harmony spans both documented flagships: a two-chord sus/maj7 vamp (vi–IV in B major, \"rather than functional movement\") and the ordinary I–V–vi–IV and vi–IV–I–V, so the vamp is authored alongside them and `susSubstitutionProb` runs at 0.34 with real sevenths. Three drum deltas are quoted: \"kick 1 and the '&' of 2\", \"hat 8ths in verse and open-hat/ride 8ths in the chorus\" (a high open-hat probability with a ride lane), and \"tambourine on the chorus backbeat\"; the fourth fact separates his electronica-leaning productions — \"a filtered 16th programmed hat runs under the kit\" — which is why the hat base is weighted rather than pinned. The bass claim is the sharpest and it is where this model differs from every artist it produced: **he plays the bass himself as well as all guitars, so bass and guitar share one rhythmic figure** — root 8ths, no fills, \"occasionally an octave lift into the chorus\", which is `mirror_kick` at 0.95 with the octave as its only passing tone. The identity is \"a short 'stringy' clean-guitar riff restated between vocal phrases\", i.e. a `riff_loop` melody with an answer-lick counter. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability and `bpm.mode` 112.",
